<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">10 events that happened on 4 February, from 960 to 2004.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/960">960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,066 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zhao Kuangyin founds the Song dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Proclaimed emperor by his troops at Chenqiao, the general became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Emperor Taizu of Song</a>. The dynasty reunited most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and presided over remarkable advances in commerce, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> and technology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Emperor Taizu of Song</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Electors unanimously choose George Washington as President</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Presidential <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> cast their votes and every one named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a>. He remains the only President to win every electoral vote, which he did again in 1792.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1794">1794 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French National Convention abolishes slavery</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Inspired by the slave revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a>, the Convention abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in all French colonies. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> restored it in 1802, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> did not abolish it finally until 1848.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/john-marshall" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-marshall.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1801">1801 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">225 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Marshall becomes Chief Justice of the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marshall began 34 years as Chief Justice, the longest in the Court's history. His rulings, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marbury-v-madison">Marbury v. Madison</a>, established judicial review and a strong federal government.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1861">1861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Seceded states meet at Montgomery to form the Confederacy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from six seceded states opened a convention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montgomery-alabama">Montgomery, Alabama</a>. Within days they adopted a provisional constitution and chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jefferson-davis">Jefferson Davis</a> as provisional President.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1899">1899 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">127 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philippine-American War breaks out in Manila</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shots exchanged between American and Filipino troops sparked war between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the Philippine Republic. Officially ended in 1902, the conflict killed some 200,000 or more Filipino civilians.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1938">1938 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler takes personal command of the German armed forces</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After forcing out War Minister Blomberg and army chief Fritsch on trumped-up charges, Hitler abolished the War Ministry and assumed direct command. Ribbentrop became Foreign Minister the same day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yalta Conference opens in Crimea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Churchill, Roosevelt and Stalin met at the Livadia Palace to plan the end of the war. They agreed on the occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, elections in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, Soviet entry into the Pacific war and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ceylon becomes independent from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> became a self-governing dominion in the Commonwealth, ending about 150 years of British rule. It became a republic and took the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> in 1972.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2004">2004 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">22 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mark Zuckerberg launches 'TheFacebook' at Harvard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Harvard student launched a social network for fellow students. Opened to the public in 2006, Facebook grew to billions of users and transformed how people share news and personal life.</p></div></li></ol>
